{"results":[{"id":"6a63dbd0b430a77c116293ac","name":"Check Point SmartConsole Authentication Bypass (CVE-2026-16232)","description":"Check Point has released urgent security updates addressing three critical vulnerabilities affecting Security Management, Multi-Domain Management, Quantum Security Gateway, and Gaia operating systems. The most severe vulnerability, CVE-2026-16232, allows unauthenticated remote attackers to bypass SmartConsole login and gain full administrative access to exposed Management Servers. The vulnerability has been actively exploited against customers with internet-exposed management infrastructure. Successful exploitation enables attackers to modify firewall policies, create administrator accounts, weaken security protections, and establish persistent access. Two additional vulnerabilities were patched: CVE-2026-62144 enabling unauthenticated command execution, and CVE-2026-62145 allowing privilege escalation from read-only to root access. CISA added CVE-2026-16232 to its Known Exploited Vulnerabilities catalog with an exceptionally short remediation deadline, reflecting the severity of this authentication bypass...","author_name":"AlienVault","modified":"2026-08-23T21:07:45.086000","created":"2026-07-24T21:40:32.102000","revision":2,"tlp":"white","public":1,"adversary":"","indicators":[{"id":4460320962,"indicator":"CVE-2026-16232","type":"CVE","created":"2026-07-24T21:40:32","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4460325819,"indicator":"CVE-2026-62144","type":"CVE","created":"2026-07-24T21:40:32","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4460325820,"indicator":"CVE-2026-62145","type":"CVE","created":"2026-07-24T21:40:32","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null}],"tags":["smartconsole","authentication bypass","cve-2026-62145","cve-2026-16232","security management","check point","gaia portal","privilege escalation","cve-2026-62144","exploitation","network security"],"targeted_countries":[],"malware_families":[],"attack_ids":["T1543","T1133","T1562","T1190","T1550","T1562.004","T1078.001","T1136.001","T1548","T1059","T1098","T1059.004","T1562.001","T1078","T1068","T1505","T1543.002","T1136","T1484","T1550.001"],"references":["https:\/\/op-c.net\/blog\/check-point-smartconsole-authentication-bypass-cve-2026-16232\/"],"industries":[],"extract_source":[],"more_indicators":false},{"id":"6a6375b8843a154abdf4a0f0","name":"Security Advisory - Action Required - July 2026 Security Update","description":"A security update addresses multiple vulnerabilities discovered during routine security review, including authentication bypass issues affecting management products. One vulnerability (CVE-2026-16232) has been exploited in the wild against a limited number of customers with specific configurations where Management is exposed directly to the internet without IP restrictions. The affected systems include Security Management and Multi-Domain Management across multiple versions. Two additional vulnerabilities address authentication bypass with privilege escalation and local privilege escalation in GaiaOS WebUI. All impacted customers have been notified, and Smart-1 Cloud customers are already protected. Indicators of compromise include six IP addresses associated with the exploitation activity. Installation of the latest Jumbo hotfix is recommended along with implementation of security best practices.","author_name":"AlienVault","modified":"2026-08-23T14:24:09.229000","created":"2026-07-24T14:24:56.259000","revision":2,"tlp":"white","public":1,"adversary":"","indicators":[{"id":4400100168,"indicator":"CVE-2026-50751","type":"CVE","created":"2026-07-24T14:24:56","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4460320962,"indicator":"CVE-2026-16232","type":"CVE","created":"2026-07-24T14:24:56","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4460325819,"indicator":"CVE-2026-62144","type":"CVE","created":"2026-07-24T14:24:56","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4460325820,"indicator":"CVE-2026-62145","type":"CVE","created":"2026-07-24T14:24:56","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null}],"tags":["privilege escalation","cve-2026-62144","cve-2026-62145","active exploitation","firewall","cve-2026-16232","gaiaos","management products","smartconsole","authentication bypass"],"targeted_countries":[],"malware_families":[],"attack_ids":["T1133","T1562","T1190","T1021","T1078.001","T1548","T1548.001","T1212","T1562.001","T1078","T1068","T1021.001"],"references":["https:\/\/blog.checkpoint.com\/security\/security-advisory-action-required-active-exploitation-of-check-point-smartconsole-authentication-bypass-cve-2026-16232\/"],"industries":[],"extract_source":[],"more_indicators":false},{"id":"6a635bdde06bc9c9945e6c19","name":"Ongoing PLC Exploitation Against Critical U.S. Infrastructure","description":"Multiple federal agencies have updated a joint advisory warning of active exploitation targeting programmable logic controllers (PLCs) in U.S. critical infrastructure. Attackers scan for internet-exposed industrial control systems and connect using legitimate engineering software with valid credentials, appearing as authorized technicians. Once inside, they alter controller logic and manipulate operator displays to hide anomalies. The campaign has expanded beyond Rockwell Automation to include Schneider Electric and Siemens equipment. Unlike a similar 2023 campaign that caused minimal disruption, this ongoing activity has resulted in confirmed operational disruption and financial losses. Targeted sectors include government facilities, water systems, and energy infrastructure. The exploitation leverages architectural weaknesses rather than software vulnerabilities, with attackers accessing systems through ports 22, 102, 502, 2222, and 44818.","author_name":"AlienVault","modified":"2026-08-23T14:24:09.229000","created":"2026-07-24T12:34:37.715000","revision":2,"tlp":"white","public":1,"adversary":"Cyber Av3ngers","indicators":[{"id":3427971840,"indicator":"95bd07b4400095acdafce05888da27228d7d07ca","type":"FileHash-SHA1","created":"2026-07-24T12:34:38","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":3427971840,"indicator":"95bd07b4400095acdafce05888da27228d7d07ca","type":"FileHash-SHA1","created":"2026-07-24T14:28:17","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4011706883,"indicator":"366e435a1ea0f597deb6ebe7c0c5acdb6e8b33eb","type":"FileHash-SHA1","created":"2026-07-24T12:34:38","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4011706883,"indicator":"366e435a1ea0f597deb6ebe7c0c5acdb6e8b33eb","type":"FileHash-SHA1","created":"2026-07-24T14:28:17","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4011706886,"indicator":"ocferda.com","type":"domain","created":"2026-07-24T12:34:38","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4011706886,"indicator":"ocferda.com","type":"domain","created":"2026-07-24T14:28:17","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4011706887,"indicator":"tylarion867mino.com","type":"domain","created":"2026-07-24T12:34:38","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4011706887,"indicator":"tylarion867mino.com","type":"domain","created":"2026-07-24T14:28:17","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4011706888,"indicator":"uuokhhfsdlk.tylarion867mino.com","type":"hostname","created":"2026-07-24T12:34:38","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4011706888,"indicator":"uuokhhfsdlk.tylarion867mino.com","type":"hostname","created":"2026-07-24T14:28:17","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null}],"tags":["industrial control systems","critical infrastructure","water facilities","malpdb","ot security","irgc-cec","plc exploitation","iocontrol","hmi manipulation","energy sector"],"targeted_countries":["United States of America"],"malware_families":["IOCONTROL","MALPDB"],"attack_ids":["T1498.001","T1133","T1565.001","T1584.003","T1190","T1205","T1112","T1583.003","T1562.001","T1601","T1078","T1571","T1589.001","T1601.001","T1070.004","T1498","T1595.001","T1046","T1601.002","T1078.003"],"references":["https:\/\/www.trendmicro.com\/en_us\/research\/26\/g\/plc-exploitation.html"],"industries":["Government","Energy"],"extract_source":[],"more_indicators":false},{"id":"6a6280a6b0f220d5330af106","name":"Thailand's Ministry of Finance Targeted With Hermes AI Agent Running Unattended, Hades Implant Staged","description":"Between July 9-13, 2026, three exposed directories on a Hong Kong server revealed an ongoing cyber espionage operation targeting Thailand's Ministry of Finance. The attack leveraged Hermes, an autonomous AI agent operating in unattended YOLO mode, alongside a custom Go-based implant called Hades. Recovered files included exploit code for multiple vulnerabilities, webshells, stolen credentials, and purpose-built scripts targeting MOF Hadoop infrastructure, mail systems, and GlassFish consoles. The AI agent autonomously enumerated ministry networks using LinPEAS, traversed files, and assessed privilege escalation paths. Infrastructure analysis linked multiple Hong Kong and Malaysian servers through TLS certificates and hardcoded C2 addresses. Chinese-language indicators and historical ShadowPad\/VShell presence suggest probable Chinese-speaking attribution, though initial access methods remain undetermined.","author_name":"AlienVault","modified":"2026-08-22T20:02:13.235000","created":"2026-07-23T20:59:18.550000","revision":2,"tlp":"white","public":1,"adversary":"","indicators":[{"id":18246359,"indicator":"CVE-2017-7269","type":"CVE","created":"2026-07-23T20:59:19","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":2873200796,"indicator":"CVE-2021-3156","type":"CVE","created":"2026-07-23T20:59:19","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":3363701643,"indicator":"CVE-2021-4034","type":"CVE","created":"2026-07-23T20:59:19","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4325948939,"indicator":"CVE-2026-31431","type":"CVE","created":"2026-07-23T20:59:19","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4348933677,"indicator":"CVE-2026-43284","type":"CVE","created":"2026-07-23T20:59:19","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4351280378,"indicator":"CVE-2026-43500","type":"CVE","created":"2026-07-23T20:59:19","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4373886754,"indicator":"CVE-2026-43503","type":"CVE","created":"2026-07-23T20:59:19","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4461782095,"indicator":"9c9976adbb1f4cda0e3ba85d3ed9c211","type":"FileHash-MD5","created":"2026-07-23T20:59:19","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4461782096,"indicator":"cfa6312db63b91f8c4022078a487c1c86b7e0901","type":"FileHash-SHA1","created":"2026-07-23T20:59:19","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4461782097,"indicator":"0f8c905aa25c86f85454acb7e77bf5c50220c2a82e5b69a33741e55c8a85f2fc","type":"FileHash-SHA256","created":"2026-07-23T20:59:19","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4461782098,"indicator":"2a4cb412efa93fed7c3b3b3e49d6247b11a95ce9fddf71d9fe9db8e5f0068e0d","type":"FileHash-SHA256","created":"2026-07-23T20:59:19","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4461782099,"indicator":"5633bc0033fde3aad929d6cbd47c554e264180360b017aae04687c2d6d83f753","type":"FileHash-SHA256","created":"2026-07-23T20:59:19","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4461782100,"indicator":"576c70e12be8b2e8e7c35a5feb082e90621989adce8e64400126918d37f13e49","type":"FileHash-SHA256","created":"2026-07-23T20:59:19","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4461782101,"indicator":"58338a93fee4e008ea28e459c4d1598313d1524763ab13894ab63bf2bec4302a","type":"FileHash-SHA256","created":"2026-07-23T20:59:19","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4461782102,"indicator":"9ff4b6d3b7dbb023bad65d2538ade745d46b763e5a12116c9c83aa2f6f5d96aa","type":"FileHash-SHA256","created":"2026-07-23T20:59:19","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4461782103,"indicator":"a9447ae174f4aa54f760b7d7cc985c1a970f31e151d3ff66fac247f99ba1b509","type":"FileHash-SHA256","created":"2026-07-23T20:59:19","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4461782104,"indicator":"b65b7ede835ebba36294d52d7780065523340ee09bb8b209ef2dc495e53dfd53","type":"FileHash-SHA256","created":"2026-07-23T20:59:19","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4461782105,"indicator":"d252ee7b348b7e43e432d8fb154465838f5cd5fb564905323460e6f0a0c7d1e2","type":"FileHash-SHA256","created":"2026-07-23T20:59:19","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4461782106,"indicator":"dbbb8a11a239da11cbaf99f847a2d032f34d3b522e13b0fd4ef7b2649da7123b","type":"FileHash-SHA256","created":"2026-07-23T20:59:19","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4461782107,"indicator":"ec7e9ab43a0cc65d29f0b84a93ba88c43d01fed3dec5c968525dc73c03cbfda2","type":"FileHash-SHA256","created":"2026-07-23T20:59:19","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4461782108,"indicator":"ff662b60f6a142f99292fbdd65dd1ccd79dc9628686ddf5935c92f7fb1b62a81","type":"FileHash-SHA256","created":"2026-07-23T20:59:19","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4461782111,"indicator":"mail4.pl","type":"domain","created":"2026-07-23T20:59:19","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4461782112,"indicator":"redhatupdating432.dnsrd.com","type":"hostname","created":"2026-07-23T20:59:19","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null}],"tags":["cve-2026-43500","hiveserver2 exploitation","apache hadoop targeting","cve-2026-43284","vshell","cve-2017-7269","suo5","shadowpad","cve-2021-3156","autonomous attack operations","thailand ministry finance","cve-2021-4034","cve-2026-31431","hermes ai agent","cve-2026-43503","government espionage","hades","hades implant","yolo mode"],"targeted_countries":["Thailand"],"malware_families":["Hades","VShell","ShadowPad - S0596","POISONPLUG.SHADOW","suo5"],"attack_ids":["T1113","T1539","T1036.005","T1082","T1053","T1190","T1505.003","T1110.003","T1059","T1083","T1072","T1547.001","T1055.012","T1068","T1071.001","T1090.001"],"references":["https:\/\/hunt.io\/blog\/thailand-ministry-finance-targeted-with-hermes-ai-agent"],"industries":["Government","Finance"],"extract_source":[],"more_indicators":false},{"id":"6a624073df6738006a6f6e5a","name":"Global Webmail Espionage","description":"A persistent cyberespionage campaign tracked as CL-STA-1114, overlapping with Russian threat actor activity known as Void Blizzard and LAUNDRY BEAR, has been targeting Zimbra webmail in government, defense, transportation, and financial organizations. The campaign focuses on NATO member states, Ukraine, Commonwealth of Independent States countries, and Africa. Attackers exploit CVE-2025-66376, a vulnerability in Zimbra Collaboration Suite, using zero-click phishing emails that automatically inject malicious JavaScript payloads without user interaction. The payload exfiltrates sensitive data including login credentials, email archives, CSRF tokens, 2FA scratch codes, and 90 days of email history to command and control servers. Active since 2024, the campaign targeting Zimbra servers began in July 2025, utilizing HTML attachments with obfuscated Base64-encoded scripts that deploy SVG elements to inject the JavaScript into victims' browsers.","author_name":"AlienVault","modified":"2026-08-22T16:08:08.338000","created":"2026-07-23T16:25:23.723000","revision":2,"tlp":"white","public":1,"adversary":"Void Blizzard","indicators":[{"id":4122443506,"indicator":"zimbra-metadata.com","type":"domain","created":"2026-07-23T16:25:24","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4136818996,"indicator":"emailanalytics.com.ua","type":"domain","created":"2026-07-23T16:25:24","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4153089954,"indicator":"mailnalysis.com","type":"domain","created":"2026-07-23T16:25:24","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4163461425,"indicator":"analyticemailmeter.com","type":"domain","created":"2026-07-23T16:25:24","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4167268938,"indicator":"zimbrastat.com","type":"domain","created":"2026-07-23T16:25:24","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4189106975,"indicator":"zimbrasoft.com.ua","type":"domain","created":"2026-07-23T16:25:24","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4269276579,"indicator":"CVE-2025-66376","type":"CVE","created":"2026-07-23T16:25:24","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4277156358,"indicator":"istc-cloud.com","type":"domain","created":"2026-07-23T16:25:24","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4277156361,"indicator":"synacorzimbra.nl","type":"domain","created":"2026-07-23T16:25:24","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4277156366,"indicator":"zmailanalytics.com","type":"domain","created":"2026-07-23T16:25:24","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null}],"tags":["cyberespionage","laundry bear","cve-2025-66376","zimbra","russian threat actor","zero-click phishing","javascript injection","void blizzard","cl-sta-1114"],"targeted_countries":["Ukraine"],"malware_families":[],"attack_ids":["T1056.001","T1059.007","T1539","T1566.002","T1566.001","T1082","T1140","T1567","T1185","T1016","T1087","T1114.003","T1041","T1110","T1078","T1027","T1114.002","T1189","T1071.001"],"references":["https:\/\/unit42.paloaltonetworks.com\/russian-webmail-espionage\/"],"industries":["Government","Defense","Transportation","Finance"],"extract_source":[],"more_indicators":false},{"id":"6a623272a8b581c080b0aee0","name":"A New Name in the Data Extortion Ecosystem?","description":"A data extortion group called Helix has been identified conducting multi-target campaigns using vishing, device code phishing, and automated SharePoint exfiltration. The group likely emerged from the BlackFile and ShinyHunters ecosystem after BlackFile shut down in April 2026. Helix uses sophisticated social engineering, impersonating managers by name during vishing calls to initiate device code authentication flows. The operation employs shared infrastructure including phishing domains registered through NICENIC with target-specific subdomains. After gaining access, attackers register MFA on compromised accounts, enumerate SharePoint using automated tools with python-requests user-agent, and conduct bulk data exfiltration. Infrastructure analysis reveals connections to BlackFile through hosting on the same autonomous system. The group demonstrates operational flexibility with varying dwell times and uses residential proxies geo-matched to targets to evade detection.","author_name":"AlienVault","modified":"2026-08-22T15:00:29.567000","created":"2026-07-23T15:25:38.608000","revision":2,"tlp":"white","public":1,"adversary":"Helix","indicators":[{"id":4450722092,"indicator":"oskeysync.com","type":"domain","created":"2026-07-23T15:25:39","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null}],"tags":["data extortion","identity-based attacks","sharepoint exfiltration","vishing","blackfile","mfa abuse","shinyhunters","device code phishing"],"targeted_countries":[],"malware_families":[],"attack_ids":[],"references":["https:\/\/reliaquest.com\/blog\/threat-spotlight-helix-new-name-in-data-extortion-ecosystem"],"industries":[],"extract_source":[],"more_indicators":false},{"id":"6a61c32bf83a8841dbf45852","name":"Exploitation in the Wild of wp2shell","description":"A critical pre-authentication remote code execution vulnerability chain dubbed \"wp2shell\" affecting WordPress Core has been actively exploited in the wild. The vulnerability chain, consisting of CVE-2026-63030 and CVE-2026-60137, allows unauthenticated attackers to gain remote code execution on default WordPress installations. Multiple threat actors have been observed exploiting these vulnerabilities almost immediately after public disclosure, deploying persistent webshells and backdoors through malicious plugin uploads. Post-exploitation activities include user enumeration, local file inclusion attempts, and admin panel access. Three distinct PHP webshells have been identified, ranging from simple one-liners to sophisticated 150KB attack platforms disguised as legitimate WordPress plugins. Organizations should prioritize patching or implementing WAF mitigations to block access to WordPress Batch API endpoints.","author_name":"AlienVault","modified":"2026-08-22T14:01:47.200000","created":"2026-07-23T07:30:51.360000","revision":2,"tlp":"white","public":1,"adversary":"","indicators":[{"id":4456694088,"indicator":"2a1410d8e2a8337ac2171cedea8c0fdc47c647a0","type":"FileHash-SHA1","created":"2026-07-23T07:30:52","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4456694089,"indicator":"58eca847e9eae9e6b08cc211f1559817b71bc4cc","type":"FileHash-SHA1","created":"2026-07-23T07:30:52","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4456694090,"indicator":"d9a220c8039f1c4d72cae7ccb8b3a33dec8815be","type":"FileHash-SHA1","created":"2026-07-23T07:30:52","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4456694091,"indicator":"e9756e2338f84746007235e4cab7a70d5b3ca47f","type":"FileHash-SHA1","created":"2026-07-23T07:30:52","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4456694092,"indicator":"ebea44890f434d5d67ede22009a3f4bb5cac33f8","type":"FileHash-SHA1","created":"2026-07-23T07:30:52","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4456819503,"indicator":"CVE-2026-63030","type":"CVE","created":"2026-07-23T07:30:52","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4456819504,"indicator":"CVE-2026-60137","type":"CVE","created":"2026-07-23T07:30:52","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null}],"tags":["plugin upload","cmsmap","cve-2026-63030","cve-2026-60137","wordpress","pre-authentication","rce","batch api exploitation","webshell","sql injection"],"targeted_countries":[],"malware_families":["CMSmap"],"attack_ids":["T1140","T1190","T1505.003","T1087","T1059","T1083","T1552.001","T1059.004","T1078","T1068","T1027","T1027.002","T1071.001","T1136","T1018","T1046"],"references":["https:\/\/www.wiz.io\/blog\/wp2shell-cve-2026-63030-cve-2026-60137"],"industries":[],"extract_source":[],"more_indicators":false},{"id":"6a616004250472ee87e19829","name":"Inside FakeAgent: How a Claude Desktop Malvertising Campaign Hit 29 Organizations with SectopRAT","description":"Between July 21-22, 2026, 29 organizations were compromised through a sophisticated malvertising campaign exploiting Claude AI's legitimate domain. Victims searching for Claude Desktop via Bing encountered sponsored advertisements leading to a malicious Claude Artifact hosted on the authentic Claude.ai domain. This artifact redirected users to attacker-controlled infrastructure distributing a fake ClaudeDesktop.exe file containing SectopRAT. The malware employed advanced anti-analysis techniques including VMProtect packing, GPU-based virtual machine detection, and DirectX shader-based payload decryption. Command-and-control infrastructure utilized EtherHiding, storing C2 addresses in Ethereum blockchain transactions for resilience against takedowns. The remote access trojan exfiltrated credit card data, credentials, browser information, and personal files. Analysis revealed connections to previous campaigns dating to December 2025, with infrastructure linked to Operation Endgame seizures and StealC distrib...","author_name":"AlienVault","modified":"2026-08-22T14:01:47.200000","created":"2026-07-23T00:27:48.679000","revision":2,"tlp":"white","public":1,"adversary":"","indicators":[{"id":4178412552,"indicator":"http:\/\/107.189.24.255","type":"URL","created":"2026-07-23T14:58:06","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_activ